.TH NETX 1 "October 2026" "netx" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
netx \- Linux network diagnostics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B netx
.I COMMAND
.RI [ TARGET ]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Commands: dns, http, tls, diagnose, check, tcp, ports, ping, trace.
Use netx COMMAND --help for syntax. Bare hostnames default to HTTPS port 443.
Use an explicit http:// URL for plaintext HTTP. IPv6 targets must be bracketed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --json
Print a schema-1 JSON report.
.TP
.B --timeout SECONDS
Timeout per step/probe (1 through 30). DNS defaults to 2 seconds per resolver
attempt; other network steps default to 5. HTTP bounds the whole redirect chain.
.TP
.B -4, -6
Select an address family (except DNS, which uses --type A or AAAA).
.TP
.B --help, --version
Display help or version.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
netx dns safal.me --type MX
netx http https://safal.me
netx tls safal.me --chain
netx diagnose safal.me --json
netx tcp safal.me --ports 80,443
netx ports --port 443
netx ping safal.me --count 4
netx trace safal.me --timeout 1
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0: all checks pass. 1: a check failed. 2: usage or internal error.
3: warnings or skipped checks without a failure.
.SH NOTES
TLS verifies hostname and trust. Use --ca-file for private CAs.
HTTP(S) checks ignore proxy environment variables and connect directly.
Ping and trace use system helpers. Missing or forbidden ICMP uses TCP fallback;
missing or forbidden traceroute reports SKIPPED. Full options and behavior are
documented in CLI_SPEC.md distributed with the source.
